          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try again , and choose different numbers this time. What product did you get? Was it different from the first time? Try a few more times with different numbers!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.146,
            0.796,
            0.167
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Play the same game with the grid below. What answer do you get?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.186,
            0.394,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.17,
                0.186,
                0.394,
                0.354
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_table_4.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>8</td><td>-4</td><td>12</td><td>-6</td></tr><tr><td>-28</td><td>14</td><td>-42</td><td>21</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>-6</td><td>18</td><td>-9</td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>-10</td><td>30</td><td>-15</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.422,
            0.235,
            0.813,
            0.313
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is so special about these grids? Is the magic in the numbers or the way they are arranged or both? Can you make more such grids?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.381,
            0.361,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Division of Integers"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.406,
            0.847,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have earlier seen how division can be converted into multiplication. For example, (– 100) ÷ 25 can be reframed as, ‘what should be multiplied to 25 to get (– 100)?’. That is,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.423,
            0.469,
            0.574,
            0.487
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "25 \\times 2 = (-100)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.493,
            0.319,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.402,
            0.512,
            0.589,
            0.531
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "25 \\times (-4) = (-100)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.536,
            0.285,
            0.555
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.408,
            0.555,
            0.588,
            0.574
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "(-100) \\div 25 = (-4)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.585,
            0.846,
            0.624
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(-100) \\div (-4)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " can be reframed as, ‘What should be multiplied to (– 4) to get (– 100)?’"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.414,
            0.624,
            0.581,
            0.642
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "(-4) \\times ? = (-100)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.648,
            0.319,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.409,
            0.668,
            0.588,
            0.686
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "( - 4 ) \\times 2 5 = ( - 1 0 0 ) ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.691,
            0.285,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.41,
            0.71,
            0.588,
            0.729
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "(-100) \\div (-4) = 25."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.735,
            0.412,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly, we know that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.416,
            0.754,
            0.583,
            0.773
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_20.jpg",
          "content": "( - 25 ) \\times ( - 2 ) = 50."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.778,
            0.285,
            0.797
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.415,
            0.797,
            0.583,
            0.816
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_22.jpg",
          "content": "50 \\div (-25) = (-2)."
        },
        {
